---
description: Read a source checkout under docs/raw/ and compile it into one cited wiki document — architecture, subsystems, and glossary, every claim citing a real file and line range.
argument-hint: [docs/raw/<checkout>/ — the repo to read]
allowed-tools: Read, Write, Glob, Grep, Bash(csdd codewiki lint:*), Bash(git -C:*)
---

## Task

Use the **codewiki** skill on the checkout at `$ARGUMENTS` (or the most recent
repository the user dropped into `docs/raw/`):

1. **Survey** it — dependency manifest, entry points, directory census, README, CI
   — before writing a word. Do not run `csdd graph`; it indexes this workspace,
   not the checkout.
2. **Outline** the full `## Structure` tree first: 6–12 top-level sections
   (Overview · Setup · Architecture + layers · one per subsystem · Configuration ·
   Development · Glossary), then keep it stable.
3. **Author** `docs/raw/<owner>-<repo>.md` section by section, reading the files
   each section covers **before** writing it. Every section carries a
   `<details>` source list, at least one `[path:start-end]()` citation, mermaid
   for anything with more than two moving parts, and tables for enums, states,
   config keys, and flags.
4. **Verify**: `csdd codewiki lint docs/raw/<owner>-<repo>.md` must be clean.
5. **Hand off** — report that it is ready for `/csdd-wiki-ingest`; do not ingest it.

Never modify the checkout, and never rewrite an existing file under `docs/raw/` —
this command adds exactly one new document. Copy file paths from the tree rather
than retyping them: a citation to a file that does not exist is the defect this
format exists to prevent.
